[36.432, "o", "Review complete. Top issue is a critical SQL injection at `demo/sample-code/users.py:7` (`get_user`), which concatenates `user_id` directly into the query — contrast with `deactivate_user` right below it, which correctly uses a parameterized query. Also flagged: a `TypeError` if `user_id` is an int, a bare `except: pass` that silently swallows deactivation failures, no rowcount check for nonexistent users, and unclosed DB connections in both functions.\r\n"]
